<LegalLayout title="Copyright Policy" effectiveDate="12 July 2026">
  <h2>1. Respecting intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Forest Network respects the intellectual property rights of others and expects members to
    do the same. Our <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> already prohibits sharing
    content that infringes another person's intellectual property or privacy rights.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Reporting infringing content</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe content shared on the service infringes your copyright, contact us at <a href="mailto:legal@theforestnetwork.earth">legal@theforestnetwork.earth</a> with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name and contact details;</li>
    <li>a description of the copyrighted work you believe has been infringed;</li>
    <li>a description or location of the material you believe is infringing (e.g. the room and approximate date);</li>
    <li>a statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorised by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law; and</li>
    <li>a statement that the information in your notice is accurate.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    We will review reports and may remove or restrict access to the reported content while we
    investigate. We will contact the member who shared it where practical.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Counter-notice</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe content of yours was removed in error, contact us at the same address with an
    explanation, and we will review the removal.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Repeat infringers</h2>
  <p>
    We may suspend or terminate the accounts of members who repeatedly infringe others'
    intellectual property rights.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p>Evan Roth — <a href="mailto:legal@theforestnetwork.earth">legal@theforestnetwork.earth</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
